course: dictionary
lesson: 2123
title: Words that move things along
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conveyor is a long moving belt or line of rollers that carries things from one place to another. Read the words around it for clues: «The things ride along on a conveyor belt, so each machine or worker does one small job and passes the thing on.» Things ride along and get passed on, so a conveyor carries things.
explain: «A conveyor belt is a long loop of rubber or metal pulled round by motors and rollers.» Motors and rollers tell you it is a machine that moves things by itself, with no one pushing.
explain: Conveyor can also mean a person or thing that passes something on, as in a conveyor of news. The clue is the word passes: the news moves from one person to the next. Always ask what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Sharks have a natural conveyor belt too. «Behind each tooth in the jaw wait rows of spares that move forward like a conveyor belt.» Here the word is used like, so it is a comparison: the shark's teeth move forward in a steady line, just like a machine belt.
fact: A conveyor is a long moving belt or a line of rollers.
fact: Conveyor belts are used in factories, airports and supermarket checkouts.
fact: «Conveyor» can also mean a person or thing that carries or passes something on.
fact: Conveyor can also be spelled conveyer, and both spellings are correct.
fact: «A conveyor belt of» means an endless stream of things, one after another.
fact: Some sharks have rows of spare teeth that move forward like a conveyor belt when a tooth breaks.
exercise: «A conveyor belt is a long loop of rubber or metal pulled round by motors and rollers.» What pulls the belt round? | Pupils | Rubber | *Motors and rollers | Sharks
exercise: Where might you see a conveyor belt? | In a bird's nest | Under the sea | On a mountain top | *At a supermarket checkout
exercise: Find and copy the word that means one thing after another in «carrying each item past the machines and workers in order». | item | past | carrying | *order
test: Dad says the conveyor at the airport is broken, so the bags are stuck. What does conveyor most likely mean? | A kind of small aeroplane | A bird that flies over the airport | A person who checks tickets | *The moving belt that carries the bags
test: What does «a conveyor belt of» mean? | A gift from a friend | A tiny bit of | A rope for climbing | *An endless stream of
exam: Ava says a conveyor is only a cat. What is the best way to check the meaning of conveyor? | Skip the word and never come back | *Put your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Ask the cat | Guess again and never check
